reviews=[
('auxiliaryCharacterSum_changeLevel_absorb','For a unit modulo full delta, the actual fixed integer-cast changeLevel API gives equality with the smaller-level character, after the true Nat-to-Int IsCoprime conversion. For a nonunit modulo delta the induced full-level character is zero, even when that n is a unit at conductor f. The original n.Coprime k gate combines exactly with full n.Coprime delta into n.Coprime(k*delta). No coprimality of k with delta or f is assumed. This first finite identity needs no NeZero or positivity hypothesis; its original finite n carrier remains unchanged.'),
('character_auxSW_expansion','NeZero f supplies the actual finite ZMod f carrier. Nonprincipal psi has true full character sum0; its conjugate sum0 cancels the exact original auxiliary AP center involving the mass coprime to K*f and denominator phi(f). The proof never substitutes an unrestricted center. Fubini is finite. For each original n, the unique residue is n cast modulo f, with natCast_zmod_val and natCast_eq_natCast_iff supplying existence and uniqueness, and the original alpha n may be complex or signed. The n.Coprime K gate is retained on both sides. No squarefree level or prime-level restriction is used.'),
('auxiliaryCharacterSum_changeLevel_eq_auxSW','Composes the preceding two exact identities at K=k*delta. The full-level nonunit deletion is still represented in that SAME K inside auxSWError, rather than silently removed when lowering the character conductor. This is an exact finite identity with psi nonprincipal, not an SW estimate premise.'),
('auxiliaryCharacterSum_norm_le_conductor','Positive delta gives nonzero conductor f dividing delta. chi.primitiveCharacter reconstructs chi by changeLevel; if primitiveCharacter were principal, map_one would make chi principal, contradicting the actual hchi. The exact expansion at f therefore applies. Unit residues have reduced natural representatives b.val, so original SW pointwise errors are used only at genuinely coprime residues. Nonunit residues vanish exactly through primitiveCharacter.map_nonunit. Norm of every remaining primitive character value is<=1 by the fixed complex norm bound. Summing all f residues costs f*E, including the legitimate f=1 edge where a nonprincipal chi cannot actually occur. Its E premise is only a finite helper budget, paid by the final public theorem.'),
('uniformAuxiliarySW_lowConductor_auxiliaryCharacterSum','The only analytic premise is the ORIGINAL publicly defined UniformAuxiliarySW F C0 with its uniform constants chosen before every atom and k,q,b. It is invoked at positive real exponent A+L and actual auxiliary k*delta, conductor q=f, reduced b. Its original divisor penalty is exactly tau(k*delta)^C0. MediumAdmissible supplies U>=1, which makes E nonnegative; the chosen x0>1 and scale>=x0 supply log(scale)>0. The hypothesis f<=log(scale)^L multiplies E with a nonnegative factor, and positive real rpow_add cancels exactly the extra L. The same C and x0 are chosen before i,k,delta,chi; no hidden extra conductor, modulus, roughness, scale, sigma/kappa or signed-residue gate is introduced. A>0 and L>=0 are the explicit public range, including L=0; no logarithm>=1 hypothesis is required for this cancellation.')]
